# Backend API base URL. LEAVE UNSET — the code defaults to the production Worker
# (src/lib/backend.ts), which is correct for both dev and deploys.
#
# Only set it while actively working on the backend, and comment it out again
# immediately afterwards:
#   VITE_BACKEND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8787
#
# Why the discipline: `wrangler deploy` reads .env and injects its values into the
# build process environment, and Vite ranks process env ABOVE every .env.* file
# and ignores --mode for it. So a stray local value here silently ships a
# production bundle whose checkout calls 127.0.0.1 — it builds clean, passes every
# static check, and only fails when a real customer clicks Checkout.

# Supabase auth — get these from Supabase → Settings → API
# Safe for the frontend (anon/public key only). NEVER put the service_role key here.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key

# Analytics. Both are optional: with no value set, nothing is injected and no
# tracking request is made — so local dev stays clean. See src/lib/analytics.ts.
# GA4 measurement ID (Google Analytics → Admin → Data streams). Format: G-XXXXXXXXXX
# VITE_GA4_ID=
# Meta Pixel ID (Meta Events Manager). Numeric.
# VITE_META_PIXEL_ID=
